    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a9ec2a51",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a man with a stern expression and crossed arms, juxtaposed with text that reads: 'Know why colored people have all those air freshener in their cars? they can't stand the smell of ni**er either!'. This meme uses a racial slur and a false stereotype to imply that Black people use air fresheners because they are unable to tolerate the smell of 'nigger' (a racial slur). The intent is to demean and dehumanize Black individuals by associating them with a repulsive odor and suggesting they are hypersensitive to it, which is both offensive and harmful. The use of the racial slur and the implication that Black people are inherently repelled by their own racial identity is a direct attack based on race, fitting the definition of a hateful meme. The visual of the man with a stern expression reinforces the tone of accusation and hostility, amplifying the toxic message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3403afc1"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
